# Line-ending policy for synproconsulting.co  (SWEB-12)
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `core.autocrlf=true` on the owner's Windows machine gave the
# working copy CRLF while the repository stores LF. That is normally cosmetic, but here
# it changed the SHAPE of the build output: the extra CR bytes inflated the compiled
# stylesheet from 4013 to 4216 bytes, across Astro's 4096-byte `inlineStylesheets: 'auto'`
# threshold. The local build emitted the stylesheet as a separate file (1093-byte page,
# 3 crawlable links) while CI inlined it (5102-byte page, 2 links) — from the same commit.
# That divergence produced the SWEB-11 defect in Sprint 2: a local measurement was written
# into RUNBOOK.md as CI's expected value.
#
# `.gitattributes` is repo-scoped and travels with the project; a local `core.autocrlf`
# setting does not, so it would not protect the next machine or the next contributor.
#
# This normalises the working copy to match the index. CI already checks out LF, so CI
# output does not change. See PROJECT_CONTEXT.md §2 and RUNBOOK.md §3/§8.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted. Git's auto-detection normally gets
# these right, but a corrupted logo or font is an expensive way to discover an edge case.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
